 "about": "The kit's sound effects, in two sets with the same labels. reel.py picks the set from the look's \"sound\" key (soft, paper or off; kitpaths.sound_set) and writes it into timing.json; mix.py plays that set. Each clip is mono, 48 kHz, already cut, faded and set to its level. mix.py plays the clips of a label in the order listed, one per event, and starts again from the top when the list runs out. gain_db is added on top of the clip's level. nudge (seconds) moves the start: negative means the clip starts that much before the event, so its audible start (or a whoosh's peak) lands on the moment.",
